;; dispositions.sexp — rv64gc-lab-v0's declared alternative dispositions (schema/dispositions.sexp; decision_the-seventeen-called.md).
;; Each states why the implementation-defined row's two arms cannot be met here and what control stands for them, before its qualification run.
;; The requirement's category stays what its source says.

(disposition (id "DS-ENDIAN") (requirement_id "REQ-D-ENDIAN") (kind case) (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (source_locator "§1.1.6")
  (argument "The specification delegates byte order to the EEI. The implementation-defined row asks for a reference configuration with a behaviour-changing control, or an observed and justified difference. The pinned binary has no key for byte order and its MBE, SBE and UBE read 0, so there is no configuration to select otherwise and no difference to justify. What that control is for, showing the comparison would see the other choice, the case's own control does.")
  (controls "the case's declared control, a big-endian byte 0, diverging at its witness")
  (controls "MBE, SBE and UBE each written and read back, so a hart that could select otherwise would differ")
  (control_property "byte-0"))

(disposition (id "DS-FENCE") (requirement_id "REQ-D-FENCE") (kind case) (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (source_locator "§1.1.7")
  (argument "The profile's reading is the one the specification states for reserved configurations, and the pinned binary has no key for fences: it executes each form this case runs the same way the laboratory does. So there is no configuration to select otherwise and no difference to justify. What a behaviour-changing control is for, showing the comparison would see the other choice, the case's own control does.")
  (controls "the case's declared control, a reserved fm that trapped, diverging at its witness")
  (controls "each of the configurations read through the next row, so a fence that trapped or wrote a register would differ")
  (control_property "fence-fm-reserved"))

(disposition (id "DS-WALK-IMPLICIT") (requirement_id "REQ-D-WALK-IMPLICIT") (kind case) (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (source_locator "§11.1.3.2") (walk_record yes)
  (argument "The specification defines the implicit accesses, and the boundary's spelling of them is the laboratory's. The pinned binary has no other scheme of implicit reads to select, and the other A and D scheme is REQ-D-SVADE's measured effect. The policy's translation rule says a successful final load cannot establish the absence of an extra access, and a GPR comparison cannot see one, so this needs more than the case: a retained record comparing what each producer's walks read.")
  (controls "the case's declared control, a walk reaching another page, diverging at its witness")
  (controls "the retained walk record: the same PTEs and values on both producers, 8 bytes each, at most 3 per walk, none written from the first walk on, each judged on every read")
  (control_property "walk-three"))

(disposition (id "DS-PARTIAL-PROGRESS") (requirement_id "REQ-GC-PARTIAL-PROGRESS") (kind case) (source_id "RVI-INTRO") (source_locator "Exceptions, Traps, and Interrupts")
  (argument "The specification leaves preciseness to the EEI and recommends it, and the laboratory declares it. The pinned binary is precise on each fault this case raises and has no key to be otherwise, so there is no configuration to select otherwise and no difference to justify. What a behaviour-changing control is for, showing the comparison would see a partial commit, the case's own control does. Faults injected at a chosen suboperation are past the reference, and stay the corpus's.")
  (controls "the case's declared control, a faulting load that wrote rd, diverging at its witness")
  (controls "each kept state read back after a sentinel, so a commit of any of them would differ")
  (control_property "load-rd-kept"))

(disposition (id "DS-ABI") (requirement_id "REQ-D-ABI") (kind record) (source_id "RVI-PSABI") (source_locator "§2.4–§2.5")
  (argument "The psABI defines the options, and the profile's selection among them is what the statement records. No hart executes an ABI: it is what the pinned compiler builds, read from what that compiler emits. So a case would add nothing. One function, a double beside an integer, tells the three float ABIs apart in the object's own flags and its own instructions: psABI 8.1 sets the flags, and under the hardware convention with ABI_FLEN=64 nothing moves.")
  (controls "CHK-ABI-NEG: five violating copies of the declaration, each refused for its own reason")
  (controls "the same function built under lp64 and lp64f, each object differing from lp64d in its flags, and lp64f's still moving the double")
  (expect (fact "object-lp64d") (value "ELFCLASS64 machine=243 flags=0x5 text=8280"))
  (expect (fact "object-lp64") (value "ELFCLASS64 machine=243 flags=0x1 text=2e858280"))
  (expect (fact "object-lp64f") (value "ELFCLASS64 machine=243 flags=0x3 text=2e858280"))
  (expect (fact "workload-flags") (value "-march=rv64gc -mabi=lp64d"))
  (expect (fact "toolchain-pin") (value "21.1.8")))

(disposition (id "DS-FP-DEFER") (requirement_id "REQ-D-FP-DEFER") (kind record) (source_id "RVI-PSABI") (source_locator "§2.4–§2.5")
  (argument "The statement says which backend was selected and how it is held, and each floating-point extension's own credit says how it behaves. So a case would add nothing. The risk is high, so the policy asks for a second method and an adversarial case: Cargo's own resolution reads the same selection a text read does, and the named negative check refuses a moved pin, a moved checksum, a missing model layer, a withdrawn qualification and shared lineage called independent.")
  (controls "CHK-GC-FP-QUALIFIED-V3-NEG: five violating copies, each refused for its own reason")
  (controls "cargo tree, a second producer reading which artifact the locked graph resolves")
  (controls "FP-VECTORS: the model layer's vectors against the spec-side exact-rational reference, a backend that moved would differ")
  (expect (fact "backend-requirement") (value "=0.2.3"))
  (expect (fact "backend-artifact") (value "0.2.3+llvm-462a31f5a5ab 486c2179b4796f65bfe2ee33679acf0927ac83ecf583ad6c91c3b4570911b9ad"))
  (expect (fact "model-layer") (value "crates/semulith-core/src/fp.rs"))
  (expect (fact "backend-consumers") (value "crates/semulith-core/src/fp.rs uses; crates/semulith-core/src/lib.rs re-exports"))
  (expect (fact "f-and-d-selected") (value "D F"))
  (expect (fact "needs-the-abi") (value "REQ-D-ABI"))
  (expect (fact "qualification-status") (value "active active"))
  (expect (fact "flag-corrections-recorded") (value "overflow/underflow"))
  (expect (fact "shared-ancestry-status") (value "active")))

(disposition (id "DS-ROUTE-FLIP") (requirement_id "REQ-D-ROUTE-FLIP") (kind record) (source_id "RVI-INTRO") (source_locator "RISC-V Software Execution Environments and Harts")
  (argument "The statement says which vehicle this unit uses and who governs its generated mirrors, and says itself that this is scope evidence. So a case would add nothing. The drift gates' own self-tests are the controls: a hand-edited mirror turns each red, and they run in every commit's gate.")
  (controls "CHK-GC-DEFINITION-V3-NEG: four violating copies, a stale mirror among them")
  (controls "the record retains one run of all three generators' drift checks, through CHK-GC-DEFINITION-V3-POS")
  (expect (fact "vehicle") (value "generated-definition"))
  (expect (fact "composition") (value "complete, 0 unbound slots, base riscv/rv64i"))
  (expect (fact "mirror-state") (value "GENERATED, scripts/gen_state.py, STATE-GEN"))
  (expect (fact "mirror-definition") (value "GENERATED, scripts/gen_definition.py, DEF-GEN"))
  (expect (fact "mirror-guests") (value "GENERATED, scripts/gen_guests.py, GUEST-GEN"))
  (expect (fact "drift-gates") (value "DEF-GEN GUEST-GEN STATE-GEN")))

(disposition (id "DS-SCOPE-CENSUS") (requirement_id "REQ-D-SCOPE-CENSUS") (kind record) (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (source_locator "§1.1.4–§1.1.8")
  (argument "The statement is about the census itself: what the scope block enumerates and how it may grow. So a case would add nothing, and that each form is executed and behaves stays EXERCISE-COVERAGE's and each extension's. The record reads the base census against rv64i-lab-v0's, which the named checks do not, and the composition against the declared scope.")
  (controls "CHK-SCOPE-CENSUS-NEG: a wrong total, and the same count with a wrong name, each refused for its own reason")
  (controls "EXERCISE-COVERAGE's DENOMINATOR LIE arm, in every commit's gate")
  (expect (fact "base-census") (value "52 forms, 40 base and 12 RV64I additions"))
  (expect (fact "same-enumeration-as-rv64i") (value "52 shared, 0 differ"))
  (expect (fact "same-source-as-rv64i") (value "yes"))
  (expect (fact "total") (value "200 stated, 200 enumerated"))
  (expect (fact "grows-with-its-fragments") (value "200 resolved in the composition, 0 differ")))
